{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"jwt-tools","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"JWT Tools","description":"Decode a JSON Web Token, see when it expires, and check an HS256, HS384 or HS512 signature with a secret. Nothing leaves your computer.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:jwtTools.decode","onCommand:jwtTools.verify","onCommand:jwtTools.expiry","onCommand:jwtTools.payloadToEditor"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"jwtTools.decode","title":"Decode Token...","category":"JWT Tools"},{"command":"jwtTools.verify","title":"Verify Signature with Secret...","category":"JWT Tools"},{"command":"jwtTools.expiry","title":"Show When the Token Expires","category":"JWT Tools"},{"command":"jwtTools.payloadToEditor","title":"Insert Payload as JSON","category":"JWT Tools"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// JWT Tools: read a JSON Web Token (header, payload, expiry) and check an HS256/HS384/HS512 signature with a secret.\n// Everything happens on this computer. Nothing is sent anywhere.\n\nconst esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');\n\nfunction b64urlToBytes(s) {\n  const t = s.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');\n  const bin = atob(t + '='.repeat((4 - (t.length % 4)) % 4));\n  return Uint8Array.from(bin, (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));\n}\nconst b64urlToText = (s) => new TextDecoder().decode(b64urlToBytes(s));\n\nfunction bytesToB64url(bytes) {\n  let bin = '';\n  for (const b of bytes) bin += String.fromCharCode(b);\n  return btoa(bin).replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_').replace(/=+$/, '');\n}\n\n/** Finds a token in text (a selection, a header line like \"Authorization: Bearer ...\", or a JSON value). */\nfunction findToken(text) {\n  const m = /eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*/.exec(text);\n  return m ? m[0] : null;\n}\n\nfunction decode(token) {\n  const parts = token.trim().split('.');\n  if (parts.length !== 3) throw new Error('A token has three parts separated by dots.');\n  let header;\n  let payload;\n  try {\n    header = JSON.parse(b64urlToText(parts[0]));\n    payload = JSON.parse(b64urlToText(parts[1]));\n  } catch {\n    throw new Error('The header or the payload is not valid base64url JSON.');\n  }\n  return { header, payload, signature: parts[2], signingInput: parts[0] + '.' + parts[1] };\n}\n\nfunction ago(sec) {\n  const a = Math.abs(sec);\n  const unit = a >= 86400 ? [Math.floor(a / 86400), 'day'] : a >= 3600 ? [Math.floor(a / 3600), 'hour'] : a >= 60 ? [Math.floor(a / 60), 'minute'] : [a, 'second'];\n  return unit[0] + ' ' + unit[1] + (unit[0] === 1 ? '' : 's');\n}\n\n/** What the time claims say, relative to `now` (seconds). */\nfunction times(payload, now) {\n  const out = [];\n  for (const [k, label] of [['iat', 'Issued'], ['nbf', 'Not valid before'], ['exp', 'Expires']]) {\n    const v = payload[k];\n    if (typeof v !== 'number') continue;\n    const iso = new Date(v * 1000).toISOString();\n    const diff = v - now;\n    let note = diff >= 0 ? 'in ' + ago(diff) : ago(diff) + ' ago';\n    if (k === 'exp') note += diff >= 0 ? ' (still valid)' : ' (EXPIRED)';\n    if (k === 'nbf' && diff > 0) note += ' (not active yet)';\n    out.push({ claim: k, label, iso, note, expired: k === 'exp' && diff < 0 });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nconst HASH = { HS256: 'SHA-256', HS384: 'SHA-384', HS512: 'SHA-512' };\n\nasync function sign(input, secret, alg) {\n  const hash = HASH[alg];\n  if (!hash) throw new Error('Only HS256, HS384 and HS512 can be checked here (' + alg + ' needs a public key).');\n  const enc = new TextEncoder();\n  const key = await crypto.subtle.importKey('raw', enc.encode(secret), { name: 'HMAC', hash }, false, ['sign']);\n  return bytesToB64url(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.sign('HMAC', key, enc.encode(input))));\n}\n\nasync function verify(token, secret) {\n  const d = decode(token);\n  const alg = d.header.alg;\n  if (alg === 'none') return { ok: false, reason: 'The token says alg \"none\": it has no signature at all. Never trust it.' };\n  const expect = await sign(d.signingInput, secret, alg);\n  return expect === d.signature ? { ok: true, reason: 'The signature matches this secret.' } : { ok: false, reason: 'The signature does not match this secret.' };\n}\n\n/** Builds a signed token (for tests and quick local fixtures). */\nasync function make(payload, secret, alg = 'HS256') {\n  const enc = (o) => bytesToB64url(new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(o)));\n  const input = enc({ alg, typ: 'JWT' }) + '.' + enc(payload);\n  return input + '.' + (await sign(input, secret, alg));\n}\n\nexports._test = { decode, findToken, times, verify, make, ago };\n\nfunction page(d, token) {\n  const ts = times(d.payload, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));\n  const rows = ts.map((t) => '<tr><td>' + esc(t.label) + '</td><td>' + esc(t.iso) + '</td><td' + (t.expired ? ' class=\"bad\"' : '') + '>' + esc(t.note) + '</td></tr>').join('');\n  return `<style>body{font-family:var(--ui)} pre{font:13px/1.5 var(--mono,monospace);background:var(--raised,transparent);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-all}\n  h4{margin:14px 0 4px;color:var(--fg-dim);font-weight:500} table{border-collapse:collapse;font:12px var(--mono,monospace)} td{padding:3px 12px 3px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)} .bad{color:#e5534b}</style>\n  <h3>JSON Web Token</h3><h4>Header</h4><pre>${esc(JSON.stringify(d.header, null, 2))}</pre><h4>Payload</h4><pre>${esc(JSON.stringify(d.payload, null, 2))}</pre>\n  ${rows ? '<h4>Times</h4><table>' + rows + '</table>' : ''}<h4>Signature</h4><pre>${esc(d.signature)}</pre>`;\n}\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  async function tokenFromEditor() {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file first.', 'warn');\n      return null;\n    }\n    const t = findToken(doc.selectedText || '') || findToken(doc.text);\n    if (!t) {\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('No JSON Web Token found. Select one, or put it in the file.', 'warn');\n      return null;\n    }\n    return t;\n  }\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('jwtTools.decode', async () => {\n      const t = await tokenFromEditor();\n      if (!t) return;\n      try {\n        await ferrum.window.showPanel({ title: 'JWT', html: page(decode(t), t) });\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('jwtTools.verify', async () => {\n      const t = await tokenFromEditor();\n      if (!t) return;\n      const secret = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'The secret this token was signed with', placeholder: 'your-256-bit-secret' });\n      if (secret === undefined) return;\n      try {\n        const r = await verify(t, secret);\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(r.reason, r.ok ? 'info' : 'warn');\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('jwtTools.expiry', async () => {\n      const t = await tokenFromEditor();\n      if (!t) return;\n      try {\n        const ts = times(decode(t).payload, Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000));\n        const exp = ts.find((x) => x.claim === 'exp');\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(exp ? 'Expires ' + exp.iso + ', ' + exp.note : 'This token has no expiry (exp).', exp && exp.expired ? 'warn' : 'info');\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('jwtTools.payloadToEditor', async () => {\n      const t = await tokenFromEditor();\n      if (!t) return;\n      try {\n        await ferrum.editor.insert(JSON.stringify(decode(t).payload, null, 2));\n      } catch (e) {\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\n      }\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# JWT Tools\n\nSelect a token (or leave the cursor in a file that contains one, like an `Authorization: Bearer ...` line) and run a command.\n\n- **Decode Token...** opens a panel with the header, the payload and the times (`iat`, `nbf`, `exp`) in plain words, for example \"expires in 2 hours (still valid)\" or \"3 days ago (EXPIRED)\".\n- **Verify Signature with Secret...** asks for the secret and says whether the signature matches. Works for HS256, HS384 and HS512. A token that says `alg: none` is flagged as having no signature at all.\n- **Show When the Token Expires** is the one line answer.\n- **Insert Payload as JSON** writes the payload at the cursor.\n\nThe token and the secret are processed inside the editor and never sent anywhere. No permissions needed.\n\n## Try it\n\nPaste `eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwibmFtZSI6IkpvaG4gRG9lIiwiaWF0IjoxNTE2MjM5MDIyfQ.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c` into a file, run **Decode Token...**, then **Verify Signature** with the secret `your-256-bit-secret`.\n"}}}